  "request": {
    "spec": "The sheet has terms: a number of days (settings, SETTING_CHANGED key=terms value=<days>), 14\nunless changed. A claim's due-by is its date plus the terms in force. A claim is overdue when it\nis OPEN and its due-by is before the sheet's today. Show due-by and overdue yes/no on each claim,\nand per person and for the sheet an overdue count and overdue-total (the due of the overdue\nclaims that count).\n",
    "prompt": "You are implementing ONE change to this application.\n\nFIRST read AGENTS.md \u2014 it states the working rules and how the app is tested, and sends you to\nDESIGN.md for the app's stack and conventions. Follow both.\n\nTHE CHANGE REQUEST:\nThe sheet has terms: a number of days (settings, SETTING_CHANGED key=terms value=<days>), 14\nunless changed. A claim's due-by is its date plus the terms in force. A claim is overdue when it\nis OPEN and its due-by is before the sheet's today. Show due-by and overdue yes/no on each claim,\nand per person and for the sheet an overdue count and overdue-total (the due of the overdue\nclaims that count).\n\nYour work is verified by an automated Playwright UI test already installed under e2e/specs/.\nRead that spec: it declares the exact data-testid anchors, values, test data and any audit\nrecords it expects \u2014 match them. Run `bin/e2e` to build the app, start it, and run the test as\nyou work; iterate until it passes. Change whatever the request needs across the app \u2014 its stored\ndata, its server and its front end. Do NOT edit bin/build, bin/start, bin/stop, bin/e2e,\nAGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md, DESIGN.md, e2e/support/ or the test spec.\n"
  },
